--TEST--
Core\Arr::countBy refuses a value it cannot name a bucket for, where array_count_values warns and silently skips it
--ORACLE-DIVERGES--
`array_count_values([1.5, 2.5, 1.5])` emits `Warning: Can only count string and integer values, entry skipped` three times and answers the empty array — a result that is missing every entry it was asked about, from a call that succeeded. `Core\Arr::countBy` refuses the call instead, which is what `Core\Arr::flip` already does with the identical situation and what AGENTS.md's ordering asks for: a silently short answer is a correctness failure the caller cannot see, and a member of `Core` does not produce one. The two languages agree on every value a bucket *can* be named for, which `arr-count-by-matches-array_count_values` asserts against PHP itself; `{by: ...}` is the way a subject PHP cannot count at all is counted here, and PHP has no function for that half.
--FILE--
<?mwl
final class Render {
    public static function counts(array<uint> $a): string {
        var $out = "";
        foreach ($a as string $k => uint $v) {
            $out = $out . $k . "=" . $v . ";";
        }
        return $out;
    }
}

// The member is working normally right up to the refused value, so the refusal
// below is about the value and not about the call.
array<string> $words = ["red", "blue", "red"];
echo Render::counts(Core\Arr::countBy($words)), "\n";

// A subject of floats, counted by naming the bucket explicitly. This is the
// half `array_count_values` has no form of at all: given the same subject it
// warns three times and answers nothing.
array<float> $prices = [1.5, 2.5, 1.5];
echo Render::counts(Core\Arr::countBy($prices, {by: fn (float $p): string => $p as string})), "\n";

// The same subject with no `by` to name a bucket. `mwl_core_arr_count_by`'s doc
// comment owns the rule: a value that is neither an `int` nor a `string` and
// has nothing naming it is where the call stops.
echo Render::counts(Core\Arr::countBy($prices)), "\n";
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECT--
red=2;blue=1;
1.5=2;2.5=1;
--EXPECT-ERROR--
FATAL: Core\Arr::countBy expected an `int|string` key, got tag 4
